# users.table: users Buildroot adds to the root (BR2_ROOTFS_USERS_TABLES,
# makeusers format: username uid group gid password home shell groups comment).
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# None. Everything on Thimsy's root runs as root (IMPLEMENTATION B.5: Nano
# runs as root and is fenced off the eMMC by thimsy-session's mount
# namespace, not by a user), and every file in the root is owned by root:
# post-image.d/10-erofs.sh writes each card's root with --all-root, which
# is only right while this table adds no user. A service that should drop
# privileges adds its user here and its files' owners in device.table, and
# then 10-erofs.sh must stop passing --all-root.
#
# One package adds a user of its own: Buildroot's dbus recipe makes "dbus",
# which dbus-daemon drops to after it has made its socket (D35bluetooth starts
# it only when Bluetooth is on). The user is in every root's /etc/passwd;
# dbus-daemon itself only in the roots of devices with Bluetooth (OA-15). Its one file not owned by root is the
# activation helper (/usr/libexec/dbus-daemon-launch-helper, root:dbus 4750),
# which --all-root turns into root:root, so the bus cannot start services on
# demand. Thimsy needs none: D35bluetooth starts bluetoothd itself (guess at
# the recipe's user and modes, from Buildroot 2025.02).
